  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Drumming, song and dance of Kamba Kua, the Afro-Paraguayan community of Fernando de la Mora on the edge of Asunción, descended from the Black lancers who followed the Uruguayan leader José Gervasio Artigas into exile in Paraguay in the early nineteenth century. Its music centres on the feast of San Baltazar on 6 January, when drummers play for the dancers, and is carried on by the community's Ballet Kamba Kua.",
